[7.9, "o", "\r\n[00:00] \u001b[1;36mSPEAKER_01\u001b[0m: So explain to me, in practice - how does your\r\n         system actually work?\r\n"]
[8.9, "o", "\r\n[00:11] \u001b[1;35mSPEAKER_00\u001b[0m: You studied organic chemistry, right? A molecule\r\n         can be written as a linear string - a SMILES string.\r\n"]
[10.1, "o", "\r\n[00:27] \u001b[1;36mSPEAKER_01\u001b[0m: And your model reads that string and predicts\r\n         whether it binds the target protein?\r\n"]
[11.3, "o", "\r\n[00:34] \u001b[1;35mSPEAKER_00\u001b[0m: Exactly. Target-agnostic - works on a protein\r\n         it has never seen before.\r\n"]
